NAME
       uname - print the kernel name, version and machine type

SYNOPSIS
       uname [OPTION]...

DESCRIPTION
       uname prints facts about the running kernel and the machine. Without
       options it prints the kernel name (Linux).

OPTIONS
       -a, --all
              Everything below, on one line.

       -s, --kernel-name
              The kernel name.

       -n, --nodename
              The host name.

       -r, --kernel-release
              The kernel release, such as 5.14.0-503.11.1.el9_5.x86_64. This
              is the version that grubby and /boot file names use.

       -v, --kernel-version
              The build date of the kernel.

       -m, --machine
              The hardware type, such as x86_64.

       -p, -i The processor and hardware platform.

       -o, --operating-system
              The operating system (GNU/Linux).

EXAMPLES
       Check which kernel runs after an update and reboot:

           uname -r

SEE ALSO
       hostname(1), hostnamectl(1), grubby(8)
